# Translation of the Museum of Alternative Displays into 한국어.
# How to work on this file: TRANSLATING.md at the top of the repository.
# 
# 한국어. The formal polite style (합니다) for what a label says, and the gentler 하세요 for what the visitor is asked to do.
# A hall is a 전시실 and a piece is a 전시품. The device as a kind is a 디스플레이, a picture surface is a 화면, a board is a 표시판.
# A name that comes out of a variable is never followed by a particle, since the particle depends on the last sound of the name.
# Large round numbers use 만 and 억 with one figure in front (1.3억 대), so that the check can read them.
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Project-Id-Version: Museum of Alternative Displays\n"
"Report-Msgid-Bugs-To: https://github.com/obartra/museum-of-alternative-displays/issues\n"
"Language: ko\n"
"Language-Team: 한국어\n"
"MIME-Version: 1.0\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"
"Plural-Forms: nplurals=1; plural=0;\n"

